NOTE (plan 11-08, 2026-10-10). `npm run soak` at its DEFAULT load (3 processes, 120 s, 100 ms write interval)
was attempted first on this host and crashed with `SqliteError: database or disk is full`: at that rate the
scratch audit.db grew to 5.5 GB (6.78 M rows) in about 90 s because every write audits EVERY row of each
collection it touches (O(N) audit rows per write, O(N^2) overall - measured identical on the pre-Phase-11 tree
13a6da0, so it is a pre-existing amplification, not a Phase 11 regression; see 11-08-SUMMARY.md finding F-5).
The host had ~5 GB free and other jobs running. The verdict below is the SAME script at a lighter write rate:
SOAK_PROCESSES=3 SOAK_DURATION_MS=120000 SOAK_WRITE_INTERVAL_MS=250 npm run soak   (D-14: same script, env knobs)
A shorter 60 s / 250 ms smoke run before it also passed (acknowledged=2044, lost=0, audit 1:1, refused=1).
